  "why_held": "The addresses the run had written while it read, and what they held. Orders are the whole chain's, so a setting read with another of the type's stages moved is a reading of something else and nothing in the numbers says so.",
  "stimulus": "a note held through the effect -- program 81 at note 45, nominally a hundred and ten hertz. This voice was chosen for being near a single partial and it is not one. Read off the take in this record made with the part routed past the effect, it arrives as two components eleven to twelve cents apart, the weaker of them two to four decibels under the stronger, and the same ratio stands at every order from the first -- which is two oscillators and not one. Two components that close beat: at this note they are three quarters of a hertz apart, so the sum swings through its whole range about six times inside a take and the stage is driven at a level that moves rather than one that is held. What this costs a reader is stated rather than left to be found. The filter these figures are read through passes one frequency, so at each whole multiple of the carrier it admits only what the stronger component made on its own -- nothing built from the other one lands exactly there. That is a definite quantity and it repeats; it is not the harmonic series a single tone through a curve would give, and a curve must not be fitted to it. What it is good for is comparing one setting against another, which is what the takes here were made for: every take in the sweep was made on this same signal",
